## Summary

Closes #3. A pass now surfaces each new finding once, so the timer does not
report success while an item waits for a person.

- `internal/reconcile/notify.go` runs at the end of a pass, after the queue is
  saved and the reboot gate has run. A finding is every item left in the queue
  plus a blocked reboot.
- `notify = "auto" | "desktop" | "stdout" | "off"` in `config.toml`, default
  `auto`.

  | Mode | stdout | `notify-send`, when a session exists |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `auto` | yes | yes |
  | `desktop` | no | yes |
  | `stdout` | yes | no |
  | `off` | no | no |

- Dedupe is by item id, state, and detail in `<state>/notified.json`, written
  under the state lock the pass already holds. A repeated identical failure is
  silent. A changed detail is surfaced. A finding that clears and returns is
  surfaced again, because its key leaves the file when it stops being a finding.
- A blocked reboot is keyed by its term. The unclaimed process names are part of
  the message, not the key.
- A desktop send failure is collected in `Result.NotifyFailed`, printed on
  stderr, and never fails the pass. The stdout line is still written, so a host
  without `notify-send` keeps converging with the journal as its record.
- A corrupt `notified.json` is quarantined and read as empty, so the damage costs
  one repeated notice instead of a failed pass.
- The session check is the reboot gate's: another login, Omarchy's stay-awake
  marker, or a `block` or `block-weak` inhibitor lock means a session exists.
- `docs/operations.md` adds the Notifications section, the mode table, the
  dedupe rule, the state file, and the pass step. `CHANGELOG.md` records the
  change.

## Verification

```text
go test -race ./...   # all packages pass
go vet ./...          # clean
gofmt -l .            # clean
```

Mutation evidence, each applied and reverted:

| Mutation | Test that turns red |
| --- | --- |
| ignore the dedupe set | `TestPassNotifiesOncePerNewFinding`, `TestPassMarksAnEscalationUrgent`, `TestPassNotifiesABlockedRebootOnce` |
| notify without checking the session | `TestPassPrintsWithoutASession` |
| never read the session | `TestPassNotifiesOncePerNewFinding` (no desktop send) |
| drop the blocked-reboot finding | `TestPassNotifiesABlockedRebootOnce` |
| stop replacing newlines in the notice | `TestNoticeStaysOnOneLine` |
| record only a successful desktop send in `auto` | `TestPassDoesNotRepeatAfterADesktopFailureWhenTheLineWasPrinted` |
| record a failed desktop-only send | `TestPassDesktopModeRetriesAFailedSend` |

## Notes

- `notify-send` is not a dependency of a pass. Without it the stdout line is
  still written, the failure is reported, and convergence continues.
- Dedupe is global per finding, not per channel. A finding surfaced to the
  journal on a headless host is not surfaced again when a session appears; the
  finding was already recorded.
- A key is recorded once anything reached the person. In `auto` a failed
  `notify-send` therefore does not re-print the line. In `desktop` nothing
  reached the person, so the next pass retries the send.
- `notified.json` mirrors the findings of the last pass that had notifications
  on. `off` writes nothing, so switching it on surfaces the findings present at
  that pass.
